---
// Internal typography test page (Phase 2). Removed before launch.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Type test" description="Internal Phase 2 page." noindex>
  <section class="wrap block">
    <p class="kicker">Puerto · type test · internal</p>
    <h1 class="headline">I study how Peru votes — and how the state delivers on what it promises</h1>
    <p class="method">
      Political scientist (PUCP). Computational social science on elections, the press and
      public infrastructure; competitive debating.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-solid" href="#" onclick="return false">View research</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#" onclick="return false">Work with me</a>
    </div>
    <p class="body-sample">
      Reconstruction after the 2017 El Niño Costero left an open question: why does what the
      state promises arrive late, or not at all? The thesis followed school infrastructure in
      Piura between 2020 and 2023, combining Mill's method of difference with semi-structured
      interviews. Every figure in the text — 747,836 headlines; 115,269 active school
      services — comes from the data, never the other way around.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .block { padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-3) var(--space-12); }
  .headline { font-size: var(--type-headline); max-width: 17ch; margin: var(--space-3) 0; }
  .method { color: var(--color-tinta-2); font-size: 18px; max-width: 54ch; }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: var(--space-2); flex-wrap: wrap; margin: var(--space-4) 0; }
  .body-sample { margin-top: var(--space-4); }
</style>
